# The only place that sizes the dev environment (ADR 0013). compose.dev.yml, compose.dev-tunnel.yml and the dev
# deploy entrypoint read these values and nothing else sets a limit; scripts/deploy/dev-model.mjs fails the pull
# request when the sum goes past the budget: 1 vCPU and 3 GiB for every long-running container plus the migration
# job, so a release never leaves the production environment of the same VPS short of CPU or memory.
# Memory limits equal the swap limits (no swap), so a runaway dev container is killed instead of paging the host.
DEV_POSTGRES_CPUS=0.25
DEV_POSTGRES_MEM=768m
DEV_POSTGRES_PIDS=200
DEV_API_CPUS=0.20
DEV_API_MEM=512m
DEV_API_PIDS=256
DEV_WORKER_CPUS=0.25
DEV_WORKER_MEM=768m
DEV_WORKER_PIDS=512
DEV_WEB_CPUS=0.05
DEV_WEB_MEM=64m
DEV_WEB_PIDS=64
DEV_MAILPIT_CPUS=0.05
DEV_MAILPIT_MEM=128m
DEV_MAILPIT_PIDS=64
DEV_CLOUDFLARED_CPUS=0.05
DEV_CLOUDFLARED_MEM=128m
DEV_CLOUDFLARED_PIDS=64
DEV_MIGRATIONS_CPUS=0.15
DEV_MIGRATIONS_MEM=384m
DEV_MIGRATIONS_PIDS=128
